# CONFIG's Advanced Params page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigFriendlyParams.cs
# in Advanced mode (ConfigFriendlyParamsAdv.cs; PLAN.md §13.6 row 71).
#
# The claim: SoftwareConfig adds the page, as an advanced page, only when the display view's
# displayAdvancedParams is on (SoftwareConfig.cs:201-204), and BackstageView draws an advanced page
# only while the view's isAdvancedMode is on (BackstageView.cs:285; MainV2.cs:601). Neither preset
# turns displayAdvancedParams on; a Custom view read from custom.displayview does
# (DisplayView.cs:442-455; here beside config.xml). A saved displayview comes back at start-up with
# the page forced off (MainV2.cs:916-925), so after Advanced is chosen and saved, the page is back
# only once Custom is chosen again on the Planner page (ConfigPlanner.cs:1018-1033) and the CONFIG
# screen made anew (MainSwitcher.cs:112-153). Showing it binds a control per parameter documented
# @User: Advanced or not at all: BARO_FLTR_RNG, which has no @User, is a RangeControl; its arrow
# records a value, and Write Params writes it (ConfigFriendlyParams.cs:179-205). The write is proved
# by the vehicle's echo, and put back.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm (BARO_FLTR_RNG
# 0). Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-advanced-params.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# A run that stops half way can leave BARO_FLTR_RNG at 1; the first expectation on it then fails
# until a fresh SITL.

env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
setup printf '{\n  "displayAdvancedParams": true,\n  "isAdvancedMode": true\n}\n' > $WORK/custom.displayview
screen params
window 1600x1200
budget 16
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

click param-download
expect params.held > 1000
# No `params.value.BARO_FLTR_RNG` here: the parameter screen records the rows it draws, and
# BARO_FLTR_RNG is far down its table. The Advanced Params page records it once it lists it.

# The file makes the start-up view Custom, with the page.
click tab-config
expect display.view Custom
expect display.displayAdvancedParams true
expect config.shown ~ ConfigFriendlyParamsAdv

# Basic: neither the page nor, isAdvancedMode off, any advanced page.
click config-page-ConfigPlanner
click planner-CMB_Layout
click planner-CMB_Layout-Basic
expect display.view Basic
expect display.isAdvancedMode false
click tab-config
expect config.pages ~ ConfigArducopter,ConfigOSD

# Custom again, and the page shown.
click config-page-ConfigPlanner
click planner-CMB_Layout
click planner-CMB_Layout-Custom
expect display.view Custom
expect display.displayAdvancedParams true
click tab-config
expect config.shown ~ ConfigFriendlyParamsAdv
expect config.titles ~ Advanced Params
click config-page-ConfigFriendlyParamsAdv
expect config.page ConfigFriendlyParamsAdv
expect config.title Advanced Params
expect config.advancedparams.active true
expect config.advancedparams.controls > 100

# Find brings BARO_FLTR_RNG to the top.
click advancedparams-find
type baro_fltr_rng
key Return
expect config.advancedparams.visible 1
expect config.advancedparams.BARO_FLTR_RNG.kind range
expect config.advancedparams.BARO_FLTR_RNG.text 0

# Its arrow records 1; Write Params writes it.
click advancedparams-BARO_FLTR_RNG-up
expect config.advancedparams.changed.BARO_FLTR_RNG 1
expect params.value.BARO_FLTR_RNG 0
click advancedparams-write
expect config.advancedparams.write BARO_FLTR_RNG 1 accepted
expect params.value.BARO_FLTR_RNG 1
expect config.advancedparams.message Parameters successfully saved.
click advancedparams-message-ok

# And back.
click advancedparams-BARO_FLTR_RNG-down
click advancedparams-write
expect params.value.BARO_FLTR_RNG 0
click advancedparams-message-ok

click config-page-ConfigPlanner
expect config.advancedparams.active false
